div></div></section><section id=3D"problem" class=3D"v3-dark inline-section=
-0"><div class=3D"v3-section-inner"><span class=3D"v3-eyebrow">The honest t=
ruth</span><div class=3D"v3-two-col-1"><div><h2>Your team is good at their =
jobs. They are just spending too much time on the wrong part of it.</h2><p =
class=3D"v3-lead">Stitching together information from different sources to =
make one decision is no longer a sustainable workflow. It is a ceiling on h=
ow fast your operation can move.</p><p class=3D"v3-body-copy">Working a sin=
gle merchant means multiple tabs before you even know where to start. Risk =
score in one place, case notes in another, transaction history somewhere el=
se. That is not a workflow problem, it is a navigation problem.</p><p class=
=3D"v3-body-copy">Most operations have accepted this as the cost of running=
 a complex portfolio. It is not. It is a solvable problem, and the solution=
 is not more screens.</p></div><div><p class=3D"inline-p-0">Investigating o=
ne flagged merchant today</p><div class=3D"v3-tab-stack"><div class=3D"v3-t=
